## Goal
Reject calls to non-existent external method overloads (e.g. 2-arg string::IndexOf).

## Source
todo-cover-cases-next.txt — Case 2 (2026-04-20, tm-control-mcp)

## Repro
```angelscript
int ix = head.IndexOf("name=\"", open);
```

## Compiler (game-side)
```
ManialinkIntrospection.as (45, 27) : error: No matching signatures to 'string::IndexOf(const string, int)'
Candidates are: int string::IndexOf(const string&in) const
```

## LSP today
Compiles cleanly (0 diagnostics). Member calls only `walk_args` — no external arity/type check.

## Acceptance
- [ ] Unique external method with known max arity rejects excess args
- [ ] `string.IndexOf(str, int)` reports no-matching-signature / ArgCountMismatch
